<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<zk xmlns="http://www.zkoss.org/2005/zul">
    <!--
        Regression sample: clipped-text must measure a text run against EVERY ancestor that clips
        it, not just the nearest one. Case B is the one that used to be missed - a roomy
        overflow:hidden box nested inside a narrow one made plainly cut text measure as fitting,
        so the LAYOUT block stayed silent about a label with a letter cut off.

        Cases C and D are single-clipper controls that were always reported and must stay
        reported. Case E fits and must stay silent, so a rule that fires on everything fails here
        too. Case A is a deliberate non-defect: a button narrower than its label does not clip in
        Chrome, the text simply overflows the border box and stays readable.

        No apply, no composer: it renders identically with and without the run-controllers flag.
    -->
    <style>
        .case { margin: 12px; }
        /* case A: button narrower than its label, no explicit overflow anywhere */
        .a-btn { width: 70px; }
        /* case B: nested clippers -- inner one is roomy, OUTER one is what cuts the text */
        .b-outer { width: 80px; overflow: hidden; }
        .b-inner { width: 400px; overflow: hidden; white-space: nowrap; }
        /* case C: known-good control -- single clipper directly around the text */
        .c-box { width: 70px; overflow: hidden; white-space: nowrap; display: inline-block; }
        /* case D: a cut of roughly 3px, inside the clipper's own box */
        .d-box { width: 97px; overflow: hidden; white-space: nowrap; display: inline-block;
                 font-size: 15px; }
        /* case E: negative control -- fits, must stay silent */
        .e-box { width: 400px; overflow: hidden; white-space: nowrap; display: inline-block; }
    </style>

    <div sclass="case"><button label="CSS Selector" sclass="a-btn"/></div>

    <div sclass="case">
        <div sclass="b-outer">
            <div sclass="b-inner">
                <label value="Clipped by the outer box"/>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div sclass="case"><label value="Single clipper control" sclass="c-box"/></div>
    <div sclass="case"><label value="Three pixel cut here" sclass="d-box"/></div>
    <div sclass="case"><label value="This one fits" sclass="e-box"/></div>
</zk>
